{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And they sat to eat bread.</b> The nine brothers." "<b>A caravan of Ishmaelites.</b> As the translator [Onkelos] said, because it goes along routes." "<b>נכאת.</b> R. Moses the Cohen, of blessed memory, the Sephardi, said that נכאת means a desirable thing, and likewise \"and he saw all her valuables/belongings\" (II Kings 20:13) [בית נכותה], for vav and alef interchange, since they are weak letters." "<b>And צרי.</b> We find it in Scripture with sheva na under the tzadi and with chatef kamatz: הַצֳרִי אין בגלעד (Jeremiah [8:22] 5:22), and also with cholam: ודבש שמן וָצֹרִי (Ezekiel 27:17). The Gaon [Saadia] explained it as that which is made from seventy-five roots, and others said it is a fruit, and others said it is a fruit or the oil of the tree that was brought from Jericho to Egypt, according to the opinion of Joseph ben Gorion, and R. Ishmael said it is a resin, and we rely on his opinion." "And לוט: the Gaon [Saadia] said it is the fruit, thus in the Ishmaelite language, with an added bet; and perhaps it is so."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {3 "Ibn Ezra's citation 'ירמי׳ ה כ״ב' (Jeremiah 5:22) does not contain this phrase; the verse about צרי in Gilead is Jeremiah 8:22. Translated the citation as given."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:22.084477525Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}